1	#!/usr/bin/env node
2	/**
3	 * source-dupes.mjs — gate `source-dupes` (contract `kumitate-source-dupes-v1`, round 56).
4	 *
5	 * The SOURCES duplicate-URL ratchet. The maintained census
6	 * (`scripts/sources-census.sh validate`) prints a W04 warning when two Registry
7	 * rows carry the same normalized URL under different scopes; it never fails
8	 * (warnings do not gate). Those warnings are the lane's own taste evidence
9	 * drifting — the same source admitted twice under different scopes splits
10	 * which row is authoritative and which `used-by` path owns the citation.
11	 * This gate promotes the warning class into a pinned, scored contract: the set
12	 * of live duplicate groups must equal the pinned `known` set — a NEW duplicate
13	 * is a regression (DRIFT), and a `known` entry that no longer duplicates is a
14	 * stale pin (DRIFT too: resolve it — supersede or re-anchor a row — and remove
15	 * the pin; silence is not a fix).
16	 *
17	 *   node scripts/source-dupes.mjs [--registry <path>] [--sources <path>]
18	 *   node scripts/source-dupes.mjs --selftest
19	 *
20	 * Verdicts (one line on stdout, after optional per-item notes):
21	 *   SOURCE_DUPES: CLEAN groups=<n> known=<n>       exit 0
22	 *   SOURCE_DUPES: DRIFT groups=<n> known=<m> bad=<k> first=<item>   exit 1
23	 *   SOURCE_DUPES: FAIL-CLOSED reason=<why>         exit 2 (could not evaluate)
24	 *   SOURCE_DUPES: USAGE ...                        exit 64
25	 *
26	 * Registry (default `.ufo/pins/source-dupes.json`, lane-root-relative):
27	 *   { "version": 1,
28	 *     "known": [ { "ids": ["S034","S050"], "url": "<normalized-url>", "why": "<reason>" }, ... ] }
29	 *
30	 * A `known` entry names the full member set of one duplicate group by row id
31	 * and its normalized URL — the census-normalized form (scheme and trailing
32	 * `/` stripped, `#fragment` stripped, host lowercased; the SAME normalization
33	 * the maintained census applies before printing W04).
34	 *
35	 * Duplicate semantics (identical to `sources-census.sh` W04): two rows share a
36	 * normalized URL AND differ in their `scope` cell. Same-URL + same-scope is
37	 * the census's E04 family, not this gate's; rows with no URL at all never form
38	 * a group; a lone row is never a group. The census tolerates same-URL /
39	 * different-scope as a warning — this gate makes the TOLERANCE explicit: only
40	 * the pinned groups may exist.
41	 *
42	 * Rules:
43	 *   - the live duplicate-group set is computed from `corpus/SOURCES.md` over
44	 *     the Registry section only (0–3 leading spaces, `## Registry` … next `#`);
45	 *     the separator row and rows outside Registry are ignored.
46	 *   - DRIFT `new-duplicate:<url>` — a live group not in `known`.
47	 *   - DRIFT `stale-known:<ids>` — a `known` entry whose members no longer form
48	 *     that group (a row was superseded/removed, the url re-anchored, or the
49	 *     scope changed so it is no longer a duplicate).
50	 *   - DRIFT `known-mismatch:<url>` — a `known` entry whose `ids`/`url` do not
51	 *     match the live group it partly covers (members must match exactly).
52	 *   - FAIL-CLOSED (exit 2, never a score): registry unreadable / not JSON /
53	 *     version ≠ 1 / `known` not an array / an entry missing ids+url+why /
54	 *     duplicate `known` entries covering the same row id; sources doc
55	 *     unreadable / no Registry section.
56	 *   - an EMPTY `known` array is legal ONLY when no live group exists; known=0
57	 *     with a live group is DRIFT, known>0 is never vacuous.
58	 *
59	 * The gate never writes. It reads the registry and the sources doc only.
60	 *
61	 * Selftest: hermetic fixtures under mkdtemp, twelve cases, one red-before per
62	 * rule; the final line reads `SOURCE_DUPES_SELFTEST: PASS (12/12)` +
63	 * `VERDICT: PASS`, exit 0.
64	 *
65	 * Exit map: 0 clean · 1 a real defect (drift) · 2 fail-closed · 64 usage.
66	 * Owner: kumitate L1. Row: SKILL.md §Gate registry (`source-dupes`, gate);
67	 * pin: SCORECARD.md `kumitate-gate-pins-v1` (`pin.source-dupes`).
68	 */
69	import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';
70	import { lstatSync, mkdirSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';
71	import { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';
72	import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
73	import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
